window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-298252b15f3a1d27"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"deploy-an-app-or-website\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">部署应用或网站</h1> <p>构建或更新 Web 应用、部署预览，并获取可访问的 URL。</p> <p>使用 Build Web Apps 和 Vercel，让 Codex 根据代码库、截图、设计稿或粗略的应用构想，构建可运行的预览版本并分享。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>根据截图、地图、设计简报或粗略应用构想，快速制作可运行的 Web 预览</li> <li>部署分支或本地应用，而无需手动配置 Vercel 命令</li> <li>在 Codex 完成构建和部署检查后分享可访问的 URL</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>提供 React、界面、部署、支付和数据库方面的指导，帮助构建、审查并准备 Web 应用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vercel（需联网）</a></td> <td>部署预览、检查部署状态、查看构建日志并管理 Vercel 项目设置。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建并部署预览版本</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 @build-web-apps 根据 [repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea] 构建一个可运行的网站。\n\n然后使用 @vercel 部署一个预览版本，并把可访问的 URL 发给我。\n\n上下文：\n- [what the site should do]\n- [source data, API, docs, or assets to use]\n- [style or product constraints]\n- [anything not to change]\n\n交付前，请运行本地构建，并确认部署已就绪。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel 部署（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-the-site-and-the-deploy-target\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">从网站目标和部署位置开始</h2> <p>Codex 可以构建或更新网站和应用、运行项目检查、使用 Vercel 部署，并返回 URL。</p> <p>交接时要提供具体材料：代码库、截图、地图、设计简报、产品说明、API 文档或数据来源。Codex 应先检查项目再做改动；默认使用 Vercel 插件部署预览版本。</p> <p>需要 Codex 构建或润色应用时，使用 <code>@build-web-apps</code>。需要它部署应用、检查部署状态或查看 Vercel 构建日志时，使用 <code>@vercel</code>。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @build-web-apps to turn [repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea] into a working website.\n\nThen use @vercel to deploy a preview and hand me the live URL.\n\nContext:\n\n- [what the site should do]\n- [source data, API, docs, or assets to use]\n- [style or product constraints]\n- [anything not to change]\n\nBefore you hand it back, run the local build and verify the deployment is ready.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 @build-web-apps，将 [repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea] 制作成可用的网站。\n\n然后使用 @vercel 部署预览，并将可访问的 URL 交给我。\n\n上下文：\n\n- [what the site should do]\n- [source data, API, docs, or assets to use]\n- [style or product constraints]\n- [anything not to change]\n\n交付给我之前，运行本地构建，并确认部署已经就绪。</div></div> <p><a id=\"check-the-result-before-you-share-it\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">分享前检查结果</h2> <p>Codex 应说明改了什么、使用了哪条命令构建项目，以及 Vercel 部署是否就绪。如果部署还需要环境变量、团队选择、域名设置或登录步骤，Codex 应明确指出，而不是假装已经完成。</p> <p>明确要求后再改生产环境。默认部署预览版本；只有你明确提出时才部署生产版本。</p> <p><a id=\"iterate-from-the-live-url\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"url\">根据在线 URL 继续迭代</h2> <p>得到预览版本后，可以继续在同一对话中让 Codex 打开 URL、修复布局问题、更新文案、接入缺失的数据，或在部署失败时查看 Vercel 日志。当前对话已包含代码库、部署和构建上下文。</p> <p>好的后续要求应具体明确：</p> <ul> <li>“手机布局太拥挤了。请修复并重新部署预览版本。”</li> <li>“沿用同一个项目，并从 [source] 添加最新数据。”</li> <li>“读取失败的构建日志并修复部署问题。”</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"deploy-an-app-or-website\">Deploy an app or website</h1> <p>Build or update a web app, deploy a preview, and get a live URL.</p> <p>Use Codex with Build Web Apps and Vercel to turn a repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea into a working preview deployment you can share.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Turning a screenshot, map, design brief, or rough app idea into a working web preview</li> <li>Deploying a branch or local app without manually wiring Vercel commands</li> <li>Sharing a live URL after Codex runs the build and checks the deployment</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Build, review, and prepare web apps with React, UI, deployment, payments, and database guidance.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vercel (online)</a></td> <td>Deploy previews, inspect deployments, read build logs, and manage Vercel project settings.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build and Deploy a Preview</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @build-web-apps to turn [repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea] into a working website.\n\nThen use @vercel to deploy a preview and hand me the live URL.\n\nContext:\n- [what the site should do]\n- [source data, API, docs, or assets to use]\n- [style or product constraints]\n- [anything not to change]\n\nBefore you hand it back, run the local build and verify the deployment is ready.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel deployments (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-with-the-site-and-the-deploy-target\">Start with the site and the deploy target</h2> <p>Codex can build or update a website or app, run the project checks, deploy it with Vercel, and return the URL.</p> <p>The useful handoff is concrete: a repo, screenshot, map, design brief, product note, API doc, or data source. Codex should inspect the project before changing it, then use the Vercel plugin to deploy a preview by default.</p> <p>Use <code>@build-web-apps</code> when Codex needs to build or polish the app. Use <code>@vercel</code> when it should deploy, inspect the deployment, or read Vercel build logs.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @build-web-apps to turn [repo, screenshot, design, or rough app idea] into a working website.\n\nThen use @vercel to deploy a preview and hand me the live URL.\n\nContext:\n\n- [what the site should do]\n- [source data, API, docs, or assets to use]\n- [style or product constraints]\n- [anything not to change]\n\nBefore you hand it back, run the local build and verify the deployment is ready.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"check-the-result-before-you-share-it\">Check the result before you share it</h2> <p>Codex should tell you what it changed, which command it used to build the project, and whether the Vercel deployment is ready. If the deploy needs an environment variable, team choice, domain setting, or login step, Codex should call that out instead of pretending the site is finished.</p> <p>Keep production changes explicit. A preview deployment is the default; ask for production only when you mean it.</p> <h2 id=\"iterate-from-the-live-url\">Iterate from the live URL</h2> <p>Once you have the preview, keep the same chat open. Ask Codex to open the URL, fix layout issues, update copy, wire missing data, or read Vercel logs if the deploy fails. The chat already has the repo, deployment, and build context.</p> <p>Good follow-ups are specific:</p> <ul> <li>\"The mobile layout is cramped. Fix it and redeploy the preview.\"</li> <li>\"Use the same project and add the latest data from [source].\"</li> <li>\"Read the failed build logs and fix the deploy.\"</li> </ul>"};
